  "id": "due-process",
  "term": "due process",
  "definition": "Due process refers to the regular administration of law through the established procedures of the courts. In this historical legal-psychiatric context, it means that a person cannot be deprived of life or property without a proper judicial proceeding, including formal claims, a chance to reply, and a judge.",
